-- SHADOW-SEMANTICS cell I15's second row, graded separately by this gate: the BARE-IMPORT
-- spelling of the same cell. A bare `import smod` binds NO names at all (its job is to
-- bring impls into scope for dispatch, which S2 governs and S1 does not), so `Sizeable` is
-- not nameable here either and the answer must match main.mdk's.
--
-- It is a distinct row because it takes a distinct arm of the predicate: `import smod.{sf}`
-- is a member list that names no interface, while a bare `import smod` yields an EMPTY
-- member list. A filter that special-cased the empty list -- e.g. read it as "binds
-- everything", the way a wildcard legitimately is -- would pass main.mdk and fail here.
import fmod.{size}
import smod

main = println (size "abc")
